@startuml
title Monte Carlo estimation as inferential statistics (MIT 6.0002 lecture 6)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
rectangle "Population\nall possible outcomes\n(every possible sequence of spins)" as P
rectangle "Random sample\nN simulated trials\n(proper subset, drawn at random)" as S
rectangle "Statistics of the sample\nmean and standard deviation" as T
rectangle "Inference about the population\nestimate +/- 1.96 x std\nwith 95 % confidence" as I
P --> S : draw at random\n(seeded generator)
S --> T : compute
T --> I : empirical rule
note right of S
  Key fact: a random sample tends to
  exhibit the properties of the population
end note
note right of I
  Valid if the estimation error has mean 0
  and is normally distributed
end note
@enduml
